WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.727
In October 2024, the Canadian Forces Aptitude Test was eliminated.

00:00:04.727 --> 00:00:12.681
The quantitative cognitive baseline — the minimum standard that ensured military personnel could process complex orders under stress — was reduced to zero.

00:00:12.681 --> 00:00:20.113
The replacement: the Scored Employment Application Form, a subjective biography-based assessment with no measurable cognitive floor.

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:22.590
The degradation timeline is systematic.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.159
In 2020, permanent resident recruitment was opened.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:31.352
In 2022, dress instructions were updated and medical restrictions relaxed.

00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:35.136
By October 2024, the cognitive test was gone entirely.

00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:38.249
Each step individually appears as modernization.

00:00:38.249 --> 00:00:44.704
Taken together, they describe the deliberate construction of a force incapable of questioning unlawful orders.

00:00:44.704 --> 00:00:47.068
The baseline was not lowered by accident.

00:00:47.068 --> 00:00:48.931
It was removed by design.
